[1;38;2;102;135;153mAnywhere[m
  (unbound)        quit, from anywhere — typing, a prompt, a picker
  ctrl+v           paste the terminal's clipboard, from anywhere
  tab              next pane
  shift+tab        previous pane
  ctrl+n           do not disturb on/off
  alt+n            mute sound on/off
  ctrl+l           redraw the screen
  ctrl+k           go to a room, person or space
  ctrl+o           back to the room you jumped from
  ctrl+i, alt+o    forward again

[1;38;2;102;135;153mAnywhere but while typing[m
  ?                this help
  q                quit
  ,                settings, showing what each is set to
  :                command line — global commands, as / is for this room
  W                why is it quiet — every rule in force for this room
  /                search this room
  ctrl+f           search every room
  @                every message that names you, newest first
  gf               every message with a file, newest first

[1;38;2;102;135;153mMoving around[m
  k, up            up
  j, down          down
  esc              open / enter pane to the right
  h, left          back / leave pane to the left
  pgup             scroll a screen back
  pgdown           scroll a screen forward
  ctrl+u           scroll half a screen back
  ctrl+d           scroll half a screen forward
  gg               the top: oldest message, or the first row of a list — with a count, that row (12G)
  G                the bottom: newest message, or the last row of a list — with a count, that row
  home             scroll to the start
  end              jump to the latest

[1;38;2;102;135;153mSpaces rail[m
  a                name this group
  K                move it up
  J                move it down
  H                hide it from the rail
  S                bring a hidden group back
  F                first names only in this space
  b                notification rule for this space
  B                give this space a key sequence to reach it by
  m                mark every unread room in this group read

[1;38;2;102;135;153mRoom list[m
  su               unread rooms on top, on/off
  sm               rooms that name you on top, on/off
  sd               rooms holding a draft on top, on/off
  s                sort by newest
  sa               sort by name
  y                accept the selected invitation
  d                reject the selected invitation
  p                list the people in this room
  v                open this room's pictures in an image viewer, newest first
  alt+r            name the thread under the cursor
  ctrl+t           list the threads in the room under the cursor
  a                name this room
  b                notification rule for this room
  (unbound)        join a room by ID or alias
  L                leave the selected room
  B                give this room a key sequence to reach it by
  m                mark this room read without opening it
  M                mark this room unread, or clear the mark
  i                invite someone to this room
  U                lift a ban on this room
  n                create a room or a space
  S                file this room into a space, or take it out of one
  A                archive / un-archive: keep the room, stop it counting
  D                read this room right to left, left to right, or as configured
  P                pin / unpin: follow this conversation, and let it through a silence
  !                spam / not spam: move this conversation out of the way, or back
  >                go to the room that replaced this one

[1;38;2;102;135;153mTimeline — message cursor[m
  i                compose a message
  ctrl+e           react with any emoji (the grid)
  alt+r            name this thread
  a                name the sender of the selected message
  b                notification rule for this sender or room
  yy               copy this message's text
  yu               copy a link from it
  gx               open a link from it
  gX               open a link from it and go to the browser
  gl               follow a Matrix link in it
  gt               read the room's topic
  *                star it, or unstar it
  H                what this message used to say
  yc               copy the verification code in it
  s                save this message's attachment
  S                save it somewhere else — opens a folder picker
  v                open this picture and the ones before it in an image viewer
  p                play this voice note, or watch this video
  r                reply to the selected message
  enter            go to the message this answers
  x                delete this message (asks first)
  E                edit this message of yours, in the composer
  e                react to the selected message
  t                open the thread this message is in (back closes it)
  T                start a thread on this message
  ctrl+t           list this room's threads
  m                next mention of you
  M                previous mention of you
  f                next message with a file
  F                previous message with a file
  [                back a day (start of this day first)
  ]                forward a day
  alt+e            write a message in $EDITOR
  zo               uncover what this message is hiding — a spoiler, or a kept deletion
  z=               correct the misspellings in the draft, one at a time

[1;38;2;102;135;153mSearch results[m
  enter            go to the selected message
  esc              close the results
  tab              widen or narrow: room → group → everywhere
  *                unstar the selected message (the starred list)

[1;38;2;102;135;153mComposing a message[m
  ctrl+enter, alt+enter send
  enter            new line in the message
  ctrl+e           browse emoji to insert
  alt+e            finish this message in $EDITOR
  ctrl+x           cut the whole draft to the clipboard
  alt+u            attach a file — what you have typed becomes its caption
  alt+s            correct the misspellings in what you are writing
  right            take a word of the completion being offered
  tab              take the whole completion, or choose from the list
  alt+m            show what the model would be sent for this draft — and send nothing
  esc              back to the message cursor
  alt+1            take the first option on offer
  alt+2            take the second option on offer
  alt+3            take the third option on offer
  alt+4            take the fourth option on offer
  alt+5            take the fifth option on offer

[1;38;2;102;135;153mCompletion popup (@… :…)[m
  ctrl+n, down     next candidate
  ctrl+p, up       previous candidate
  tab, enter       insert the selected candidate
  esc              close the popup

[1;38;2;102;135;153mCorrecting a misspelling[m
  s, space         leave this word, go to the next (space too)
  a                add it to your dictionary — kept after a restart
  i                accept it for this session
  esc              stop, leaving the rest underlined
  1                take the first suggestion and go to the next word
  2                take the second suggestion and go to the next word
  3                take the third suggestion and go to the next word
  4                take the fourth suggestion and go to the next word
  5                take the fifth suggestion and go to the next word
  6                take the sixth suggestion and go to the next word
  7                take the seventh suggestion and go to the next word
  8                take the eighth suggestion and go to the next word
  9                take the ninth suggestion and go to the next word

[1;38;2;102;135;153mEmoji browser[m
  enter, tab       insert the selected emoji
  esc              close the browser

[1;38;2;102;135;153mChoosers (people, identities, colors)[m
  i                start typing to narrow the list
  a                name the person under the cursor
  r                remove the person under the cursor from this room
  b                ban the person under the cursor from this room
  alt+r            name the thread under the cursor
  space            tick the row under the cursor (in a list of checkboxes)
  enter, tab       choose the item under the cursor, or apply the ticked ones
  esc              stop typing, then close

[1;38;2;102;135;153mReacting[m
  enter            post the typed reaction
  esc              close the prompt
  1                react with the palette's first emoji
  2                react with the palette's second emoji
  3                react with the palette's third emoji
  4                react with the palette's fourth emoji
  5                react with the palette's fifth emoji
  6                react with the palette's sixth emoji
  7                react with the palette's seventh emoji
  8                react with the palette's eighth emoji
  9                react with the palette's ninth emoji
  0                react with the palette's tenth emoji

[1;38;2;102;135;153mVoice note playing[m
  space            play / pause (from the end, plays it again)
  [                back by the skip step
  ]                forward by the skip step
  {                slower
  }                faster
  =                back to the speed set for this place
  w                remember this speed for a room, a space or a person
  P                stop and close the player

[1;38;2;102;135;153mAt a prompt[m
  tab              widen or narrow: room → space → everywhere
  enter            accept what you typed
  esc              close the prompt

[1;38;2;102;135;153mConfirming[m
  y                go ahead
  n, esc           never mind

[1;38;2;102;135;153mDevice verification[m
  y                accept / confirm the emoji match
  n, esc           reject

[1;38;2;102;135;153mEditing text (in any field)[m
  left             one character left
  right            one character right
  ctrl+left, alt+left, alt+b one word left
  ctrl+right, alt+right, alt+f one word right
  home, ctrl+a     to the start
  end, ctrl+e      to the end
  backspace        delete the character before the caret
  delete           delete the character after it
  ctrl+w, ctrl+backspace, ctrl+h, alt+backspace delete the word before it
  ctrl+delete, alt+d delete the word after it
  ctrl+u           delete everything before it
  ctrl+k           delete everything after it
  ctrl+z           undo
  ctrl+r           redo
  up               one row up (in the composer)
  down             one row down (in the composer)
  a field's own binding wins: ctrl+e browses emoji in the composer,
  because [keys] puts it there.
  home and end are the line's ends in a field, not the timeline's.

[1;38;2;102;135;153mTyped into the composer[m
  /me <what you are doing>       send as an emote — “* you wave” rather than “you: waves”
  /summary [2h | 7d | yesterday | 2026-09-18 | 50] what this room has been saying — since you last read it, or over the span you name
  /plain <message>               send it exactly as typed — no Markdown, no rendering
  /upload <path[ | caption]>     send a file, with words under it if you add them
  /at <time> <message>           send it later today — /at 09:00 good morning
  /in <delay> <message>          send it after a delay — /in 2h see you then
  /tracked [word]                where your tracked words came up here — tab widens, no word groups them
  /files                         every message with a file in this room — tab widens it
  /mentions                      where you were named in this room — tab widens it
  /search [terms]                search this room — tab widens it, no terms just opens the box
  /threads                       the conversations in this room — the same list `ctrl+t` opens
  /starred                       what you have starred here — tab widens it, and it unstars too
  /scheduled                     what is waiting to go out in this room — enter cancels one
  /topic                         what this room is for, in full — the same reader `gt` opens
  /why                           why this room does or does not notify you — the whole rule chain
  /unread                        mark this room unread — read, and still needs you
  /pin                           follow this conversation — it joins Pinned and can be let through a silence
  /caught                        what the spam filters catch here — tab widens it
  /spam                          move this conversation into Spam, or take it out — out of the counts, still readable
  /direction                     read this room right to left, then left to right, then as [display.direction] says
  /archive                       stop this room counting toward anything unread — it stays readable
  /invite <@user:server>         invite somebody to the room you are writing in
  /leave                         leave the room you are writing in (asks first)
  //text            sends a literal leading slash
  anything else starting with a slash is a message that starts with a slash

